  <title>Product name cleanup</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Product name cleanup</gui></guiseq>
  checks every product name against your naming rules, such as how units are
  spelled and capitalised, and fixes the names you choose. The same rules flag
  a name as it is typed in <link xref="product_edit_main"/>.</p>

  <p>The first time, click <gui>Set up name rules</gui>. This adds a starting
  set of rules for you to edit. Nothing is renamed until you apply a fix.</p>

  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Fixes</gui></title>
    <p>Each name that breaks a rule, the <gui>Problem</gui>, and the
    <gui>Suggested name</gui>. Check <gui>Fix</gui> on those to rename, or
    <gui>Select all</gui>, and click <gui>Apply selected fixes</gui>.
    <gui>Refresh</gui> reads the rules again and scans every name, clearing
    the checks.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Word order</gui></title>
    <p>Names with the brand somewhere other than the front, where the rest
    lead with it. These are for you to fix by hand; right click one for its
    <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Duplicates</gui></title>
    <p>Names that are the same once capitals and spacing are ignored, and so
    probably one part entered twice. They are not merged here, because
    invoices and orders point at a particular product.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Rules</gui></title>
    <p>The rules themselves. <gui>Variants</gui> are the spellings to replace,
    separated by commas; <gui>Canonical</gui> is what they become. Changing a
    rule rescans the <gui>Fixes</gui> tab. <gui>New rule</gui> adds one;
    <gui>Remove rule</gui>, or unchecking <gui>On</gui>, turns one off and
    keeps it off.</p></item>
  </terms>

</page>
